abstract: "An explicit negative answer to Kurose's printed Question 3(e) using S^2(1) times R with its Levi-Civita connection. Radial orthogonal distributions are integrable, but the dual statistical structure is nowhere locally 1-conformally flat. Includes a non-self-dual extension, direct proof, exact checkers, and a bounded priority audit. Historical priority is unresolved because relevant sources remain uninspected; no first-resolution claim or assertion of continued open status is made."
